<title>GREECE: BEFORE THE BELL: AEGEK, VIOTER TRADE EX-DIV TUES.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL: AEGEK, VIOTER TRADE EX-DIV TUES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of construction firm Aegek</p>
<p>and Vioter will trade ex-dividend on</p>
<p>Tuesday. The respective dividends per share: Aegek 70, Vioter</p>
<p>21.</p>
<p>Also on Tuesday, Gnomon's rights begin trading at 15</p>
<p>drachmas. The last day of trading in Gnomon's 8.0 million rights</p>
<p>is July 17. The minimum lot is 10 rights.</p>
<p>Vector will also trade ex-dividend and under the new name</p>
<p>Halkor. Halkor's 25,554,961 rights will start trading at 99</p>
<p>drachmas. The minimum lot is 10 rights.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange said the adjusted starting prices</p>
<p>for the above shares will have as follows:</p>
<p>    Aegek		  1,530  drachmas</p>
<p>    Aegek pref	   1,135</p>
<p>    Bioter		   529</p>
<p>    Halkor		 2,845</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
